  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer planar dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45° incidence using TiO2 (high index) and SiO2 (low index) in alternating sequence starting with TiO2. Initialize all layer thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 550nm center wavelength (approximately 57nm TiO2, 96nm SiO2). Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with bounds of ±25nm around initial values. Maximize a composite objective: mean reflectance over 450-650nm band plus mean transmittance over 700-1000nm band, with equal weighting. Incident medium is air. Evaluate both s and p polarization states and report unpolarized average performance. Total layer count is exactly 24 finite layers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica at 45° incidence to maximize reflectance in 450-650 nm and transmittance in 700-1000 nm, while suppressing leakage in the opposite bands, using gradient-based thickness optimization with ±25 nm bounds from quarter-wave initialization at 550 nm.",
